If you have ever used a chat app, multiplayer game, or live notification system, you’ve experienced the magic of real-time communication.
Traditionally, web apps relied on HTTP requests, where the client asks the server for data and waits for a response.
This works fine for static websites, but it’s too slow and inefficient for real-time features.
That’s where WebSockets come in.
WebSockets provide a persistent, two-way connection between the client and the server.
Once established, both sides can send messages to each other instantly without constantly reloading or polling the server. This makes WebSockets perfect for chat applications.

