Of course, this is just the beginning. A real-world chat app would include user authentication, message history stored in a database, private chat rooms, and possibly typing indicators or read receipts.
But the core of it all is the same: a WebSocket connection that keeps your clients and server in constant communication.
WebSockets make modern real-time web applications possible, and Node.js provides the perfect environment for building them—fast, lightweight, and event-driven.
If you’re building a chat app, live feed, or multiplayer game, WebSockets should be one of the first tools you reach for.
